e from the move list, the best practical winning try is to activate the rook to the kingside where White’s king is cramped. The rook swing also keeps flexibility: next Black can consider …h6 to open lines, or …g6 to undermine g5/h5, while knights and king support the attack.\n\nAnswer: R: a8-h8'}
